  "articleBody": "Rushing through wall repairs after heavy weather can lead to trapped dampness, ruined finishes, and wasted money. Keep an eye out for these frequent mistakes when addressing wet sheetrock.\n\nCovering wet drywall with fresh material: Trapping lingering moisture behind new boards encourages mold. Strip out damaged sections instead.\n\nStarting finish work before fixing the leak: Painting or patching before stopping roof or siding penetrations ensures failures will return during the next rain.\n\nSkipping cavity insulation checks: Drywall often dries on the surface while fiberglass insulation behind it holds gallons of water against wall studs. Always open and inspect.\n\nRelying on standard household fans: Regular fans blow humid air around without extracting moisture. Use commercial dehumidifiers and air movers, and verify drying with moisture meters compared against dry control areas.\n\nDisturbing visible microbial growth without containment: Ripping out contaminated drywall spreads spores throughout unaffected living spaces. Contain the area before cutting.\n\nAssuming touch confirms dryness: Cool walls often deceive your hands. Demand recorded moisture readings before closing up any wall cavity.\n\nWhat to Do Next: HH Remodeling LLC provides hands-on storm damage restoration, drywall replacement, and finish repairs throughout the Denver metro area. Call 303-505-0866 to discuss your repair plan with Abraham Becerra.",
  "datePublished": "2026-10-23"
